    "summary": "High‑energy rock set highlighted by Comes A Time and tight Casey Jones",
    "blurb": "The show delivers a hard‑rock first half with standout performances of 'Comes A Time', 'Cumberland Blues' and an explosive 'Casey Jones' opener. Jerry’s vocals are expressive while Keith’s piano adds fresh texture; the rhythm section drives a tight, high‑energy flow throughout.",
    "review": "On October 27 1971 at the Onondaga County War Memorial the Dead were firing on all cylinders. The band kicks off with an explosive 'Casey Jones' that lets Bill Kreutzmann’s drumming sparkle like fireworks, then rolls through a rock‑charged first set featuring a gorgeous, breath‑taking rendition of 'Comes A Time' and a tight, riff‑laden 'Cumberland Blues'. Keith Godchaux’s piano is right in the pocket, adding new color to the newer material while Jerry’s voice carries both grit and tenderness. The second set stays locked in, with 'Bertha' and a crisp 'Truckin'' leading into a seamless Not Fade Away > Goin’ Down The Road Feeling Bad medley that caps the night on an exhilarating high. All three available soundboard recordings capture the performance brilliantly, but the Miller SBD (gd1971-10-27.sbd.miller.32668.sbeok.flac16) offers pristine stereo clarity that lets every nuance shine.",
